    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 3/3 tests passing). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization for owner creation in the OfficeFloor `POST /api/owners` pipeline.\n\n**New utility \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java`** (a plain util, mirroring `E164Telephone`):\n- Trims and collapses internal whitespace to single spaces\n- Upper-cases\n- Expands whole-token abbreviations: `ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`\n- Returns `\"\"` for null/blank input (so it works both as a normalizer and safely in comparisons)\n\n**`RequireOwnerFields.java`** \u2014 normalizes the address *in place* as the first thing the entry step does, before the required-field check. This means:\n- The blank check now rejects an address that is blank *after* normalization (400).\n- The normalized value is republished on the body, so `BuildOwner` maps it onto the `Owner` and it's stored and returned normalized.\n\n**`RejectDuplicateHousehold.java`** and **`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 both address comparisons (household duplicate detection and the shared household id derivation) now run through `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)` on both sides, so the normalized form drives duplicate detection and the deterministic `householdId`.\n\nBecause normalization must precede the address required-field check, and only the first step may bind `@RequestBody`, it belongs in `RequireOwnerFields` rather than a separate `Normalize` step (unlike telephone/email, whose blank checks operate on the raw value).\n\nThe three new acceptance tests pass: whitespace/case collapse (`  12  main  st ` \u2192 `12 MAIN STREET`), abbreviation expansion (`7 elm ave` \u2192 `7 ELM AVENUE`), and blank-after-normalize rejection (`   ` \u2192 400).",
